## Findings

### High — Pi process continuity across `/reload` remains unverified

The Round 2 process-continuity finding is only partially addressed. The revised harness now proves that each process group is empty after `/quit`, but the reload section still compares only `foreground_process_group_id`. It prints `pi_info_before_reload` and `pi_info_after_reload` without asserting that the same Pi host PID and command remain. A replacement process can join the existing foreground process group, so the commands still do not prove the whole-run claim of “one Pi process … across `/reload`.”

Identify the Pi host process from `foreground_processes` after launch, retain its PID and command/argv, and assert that exact host process is present and unchanged both before and after `/reload` (while continuing to check the process group, single peer, and single status).

### Medium — The advertised media-provider fallback still cannot run the harness

Section A still accepts `nowplaying-cli` when `media-control` is absent, then immediately invokes `media-control`; all subsequent state helpers also require it. The dependency text’s suggestion to adapt the helper does not make the provided verification self-contained. Require `media-control` unconditionally, or include and select a complete tested implementation for the fallback.
